title: Route1NotebookStart
tags: cutscene
---
// The entry node of box R1Notebook, started by going to work after the knock night
// (door_3b_inside.yarn); free time (R1Free2) has no scene. Evening: he comes home to 3B.
// Her notebook is on the kitchenette counter, his only table.
<<enter_box R1Notebook>>
<<fade_out>>
<<hide Samantha>>
<<place Player PlayerInto3B>>
<<face Player right>>
<<card "Evening.">>
<<fade_in>>
You: Home. Finally.
You: The light's on. I switched it off this morning.
<<note r1_nb "Something's on the kitchenette counter.">>
// The player walks freely from here. The notebook is on the kitchenette (kitchen_3b.yarn).
===
title: Route1NotebookRead
tags: cutscene
---
// Started by reading her pages at the kitchenette (kitchen_3b.yarn).
<<done R1Notebook read>>
You: Her handwriting. Small, even, no crossings-out.
You: A page for the viewing. "Keen to please. Waits to be told. Doesn't know it yet."
You: Thursday. "Brought the right wine. Shoes off before I asked."
You: And a new page. Dated the night she knocked.
You: "Answered on the first knock. Stood where I put him."
You: "Reached once. Stopped when told. Didn't sulk."
You: "Went red when I said good. Pretended he hadn't."
You: ...I did not go red.
You: One more line, underlined. "Ask him what he liked. He won't say it unprompted."
// Three knocks.
You: Someone's at my door.
<<note r1_nb "Answer the door.">>
// The player walks to the front door. Answering it starts Route1NotebookAsk (door_3b_inside.yarn).
===
title: Route1NotebookAsk
tags: cutscene
---
// Started by answering the door after reading her pages (door_3b_inside.yarn). She let
// herself in with the spare key earlier, and made the notebook a conversation on purpose.
<<place Samantha SamanthaWait>>
<<show Samantha>>
<<open_door Door3B>>
<<face Samantha Player>>
<<face Player Samantha>>
{$samantha_name}: You read it.
You: It was on my counter. You left it there.
{$samantha_name}: I did. With the spare key. I keep it, remember.
{$samantha_name}: I could have told you what I wrote. This way I get to watch your face.
<<walk Samantha SamanthaToKitchen no_wait>>
<<walk Player PlayerToKitchen>>
<<await_walks>>
<<close_door Door3B>>
<<face Samantha Player>>
<<face Player Samantha>>
{$samantha_name}: Sit if you like. This is a talk, not a test.
{$samantha_name}: The other night. What did you like?
You: ...All of it?
{$samantha_name}: Try again. Properly.
You: Being told to wait.
{$samantha_name}: Mm. And?
You: That you didn't hurry.
{$samantha_name}: And the thing you wouldn't say out loud?
You: ...
{$samantha_name}: I'll wait. I'm good at it.
<<done R1Notebook ask>>
<<note r1_nb "Tell her what you liked. And what you wouldn't say.">>
// The player is in control: telling her starts Route1NotebookLimits (samantha_3a.yarn).
===
title: Route1NotebookLimits
tags: cutscene
---
// Started by telling her what he liked (samantha_3a.yarn). Limits first, then her first
// step towards his receptive side, kept light.
<<done R1Notebook limits>>
{$samantha_name}: You don't have to say it all at once.
{$samantha_name}: Rules first. Mine, for this.
{$samantha_name}: Three answers. Yes, not yet, no. All three are fine.
{$samantha_name}: Being told what to do.
You: Yes.
{$samantha_name}: I know. Being told when to wait.
You: Yes.
{$samantha_name}: Your hands held down. By me.
You: ...Not yet.
{$samantha_name}: Good. Not yet is allowed.
{$samantha_name}: Being hurt.
You: No.
{$samantha_name}: Noted. I don't want that either. I want you listening, not flinching.
{$samantha_name}: And the thing you wouldn't say.
You: ...That I didn't want to be the one reaching. Last night. That I wanted to be the one reached for.
{$samantha_name}: Ah.
{$samantha_name}: That's in the notebook too. Page three.
{$samantha_name}: I'd like to find out how far that goes. Slowly. With you telling me when to stop.
You: Slowly.
{$samantha_name}: Yes, not yet or no?
You: ...Yes. A little.
{$samantha_name}: A little. Good.
{$samantha_name}: A word, then. If you say it, everything stops. No questions, no sulking.
{$samantha_name}: Croissant.
You: Croissant?
{$samantha_name}: You'll never say it by accident. You'll never forget it either.
You: ...Croissant.
{$samantha_name}: And I can say it too. Remember that.
// She puts her hand flat on his chest. Warm. She watches him breathe.
{$samantha_name}: Tonight was for talking. Mostly.
{$samantha_name}: You're blushing, and I like it. Do you want to find out what "a little" is?
You: ...Yes.
{$samantha_name}: Then go and lie down. On your front.
<<wait 1>>
<<fade_out>>
// Her first step with his receptive side, on a dark screen until it has scene art:
// a little, slow, talked through, the safeword in reach.
// Scene art, later: him on his front on the mattress, her kneeling beside him.
{$samantha_name}: Pillow under your hips. There.
{$samantha_name}: Tell me what you're thinking.
You: That I don't know what I'm doing.
{$samantha_name}: You don't have to. I do.
// She runs her hand down his back, slowly, and leaves it resting low.
{$samantha_name}: I brought something. It's cold for a second.
You: You brought it? You planned this?
{$samantha_name}: I plan everything. You're in the notebook, remember.
// A cool touch. One finger, resting, not pushing.
{$samantha_name}: Breathe out.
You: ...
{$samantha_name}: Yes, not yet or no?
You: Yes.
// She presses in, a little. Slowly. She stops and waits.
{$samantha_name}: Still yes?
You: Still yes.
{$samantha_name}: Good. That's a little. Here's a little more.
// Deeper. She curls her finger, and he makes a sound he didn't know he could make.
{$samantha_name}: Oh. There it is.
You: What... was that?
{$samantha_name}: That was you, finding out.
{$samantha_name}: Don't hide your face. I want to hear you.
// She keeps the same slow rhythm and reaches round to hold him with her other hand.
// She doesn't stroke. She just holds him while she moves inside him.
You: I'm close.
{$samantha_name}: I know. Your whole back just told me.
{$samantha_name}: Not yet.
You: Please.
{$samantha_name}: You remember the word?
You: Yes.
{$samantha_name}: You don't need it, do you.
You: No.
{$samantha_name}: Then wait for me to say.
// She keeps him there, a long moment, her mouth by his ear.
{$samantha_name}: Good. Now.
// He comes in her hand, with her still inside him, shaking.
<<wait 1>>
{$samantha_name}: Breathe. I've got you.
// She stays like that until he's still, then slowly lets go.
{$samantha_name}: That was a little.
You: That was a little?
{$samantha_name}: Mm. Get some water. I'm going to write.
<<wait 1>>
<<fade_in>>
// She writes at the counter, then reads it out.
{$samantha_name}: "Said 'a little.' Meant 'more'."
{$samantha_name}: One line longer.
{$samantha_name}: Goodnight, boyfriend.
<<open_door Door3B>>
<<walk Samantha SamanthaToLanding>>
<<hide Samantha>>
<<close_door Door3B>>
<<wait 1>>
<<note r1_nb "Go to bed.">>
You: Boyfriend. I still haven't got used to it.
// The player is in control in 3B. Going to bed is the exit (bed_3b.yarn).
===
title: Route1NotebookEnd
tags: cutscene
---
// Started by going to bed after the notebook (bed_3b.yarn): the end of route 1 so far.
// The exit leads to R1HerWorld, a stub.
<<fade_out>>
<<card "Her notes, one line longer.">>
<<end_demo>>
===
